# A6 — GitNexus graph refresh cron (FR-MEM-6 / NFR-OBS-5; story:
# _bmad-output/sprint-artifacts/dark-factory-v6/stories/a6-gitnexus-refresh-cron.md).
# Install (operator, on the VPS, as the deploy user):
#   crontab deploy/vps/crontab.factory
# Cadence: 5h — inside FR-MEM-6's 4–6h window; one missed cycle still fits
# the 8h staleness ceiling. Minute 7 keeps the tick off the top of the hour.
# Prerequisites (one-time, operator):
#   mkdir -p /var/log/qds   — root-owned so only the deploy user's writes land
#     there; AND the log FILE itself must exist and be writable by the deploy
#     user (a root-owned 755 dir blocks the deploy user from CREATING the log
#     at redirect-open time — the same silent pre-wrapper entry death warned
#     about below), so hand it over after the mkdir:
#       install -o deploy -m 0644 /dev/null /var/log/qds/refresh-cron.log
#   bun on the host         — the wrapper resolves it itself (PATH probe, then
#     ~/.bun/bin, /usr/local/bin, ~/.local/bin); do NOT add a PATH= line here:
#     cron env values are literal (no shell expansion), so a PATH copied from
#     an interactive shell rots silently — the wrapper's probe list is the
#     durable resolver.
# Env contract, stage order, and exit codes live in the wrapper header:
#   scripts/gitnexus-refresh.sh
SHELL=/bin/bash
7 */5 * * * /opt/qds-factory/scripts/gitnexus-refresh.sh >> /var/log/qds/refresh-cron.log 2>&1

# A3 — maintenance sweep pass (story:
# _bmad-output/sprint-artifacts/dark-factory-v6/stories/a3-maintenance-sweeps-f4.md).
# A6 owns this file; A3 owns the entry below (A1's documented-crontab-line
# precedent). Weekly, Monday 03:17 box-local (UTC on the VPS) — off the top of
# the hour, and off A6's minute 7. The pass is bounded and EXITING: it reads
# the graph under a SHARED flock on A6's .refresh.lock (a mid-refresh tick is a
# counted skip), submits at most 5 briefs through `fleet submit`, persists its
# report record under .sandbox/maintenance/sweep-reports/, and exits 0 on every
# per-brief refusal (exit table: scripts/maintenance-sweep.ts header).
# Prerequisites (one-time, operator):
#   install -o deploy -m 0644 /dev/null /var/log/qds/maintenance-sweep.log
#   config/manager.json — A1's config of record (the Maintenance bot id)
#   gitnexus on the PATH above or at ~/.local/node-arm64/bin (else the graph
#     leg is a counted, named graph-unavailable and the sweep runs audit-only)
#   DF3.8's completion sweep — submitted briefs reach the approve gate ONLY
#     when `fleet observe --all` drives DF3.7's chain. That schedule is the
#     OPERATOR's own cron (DF3.8 INV-IBOX-19: documented, never installed);
#     `bun scripts/fleet.ts observe --help` prints the line. Without it,
#     sweep runs stay `running` and never park.
#   .factory/ on the host — the reverify host plan and the approvers
#     allowlist the chain's gate step reads (operator-local, gitignored);
#     without them a finished run stops at `pausing`, never `awaiting-approval`.
# Install note: `crontab <file>` REPLACES the deploy user's whole crontab.
#   Operator-owned lines (A1's manager digest, DF3.8's observe sweep) must be
#   merged, e.g.  (crontab -l; cat deploy/vps/crontab.factory) | crontab -
#   after removing any stale copies of this file's entries.
# PATH: a Debian cron PATH is /usr/bin:/bin — no bun. The pass and every child
# it spawns (fleet CLI, staleness reader) need bun, so the entry prepends the
# same three locations gitnexus-refresh.sh probes, INLINE: shell-expanded at
# fire time, unlike a literal PATH= cron line (the rot warned about above).
17 3 * * 1 cd /opt/qds-factory && PATH="$HOME/.bun/bin:/usr/local/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH" bun scripts/maintenance-sweep.ts >> /var/log/qds/maintenance-sweep.log 2>&1
